text:
The vishalakshi command runs vault methods from a shell, for example vishalakshi grab https://example.com/post or vishalakshi ask "why does late chunking help". CMDS lists the methods it offers. Each one becomes a subcommand through cmd, which builds the subcommand’s arguments from the method’s signature, so vishalakshi search --help shows the same parameters and descriptions as the documentation. Arguments that cannot be typed on a command line, such as a function or a stand-in chat, are left out. Every command opens the same vault: the file $VISHALAKSHI_VAULT names, else ~/.vishalakshi/vault.db, and $VISHALAKSHI_OFFLINE keeps it from downloading a model. A result is printed as JSON, except an answer, which is printed as prose with its citations.
